Security hardening against hostile devices and files: secrets (passwords, SNMP communities, Elasticsearch URL credentials) are no longer recorded in results files, auto-generated configs or the ``peat-configs`` index, and results created by the CLI are only accessible to the user running PEAT; content-derived device identifiers can no longer escape the results directory; SSH reads, M340/ControlLogix/SNMP/GE D25 pulls and UMAS frame reads are bounded by size, count and wall-clock deadlines; zlib data inflated while parsing (M340, ControlLogix, SEL CID checks) is size-limited; the Woodward ``.wset`` reader validates counts and caps its output; config encryption uses a random salt per file (``PEAT_CRYPT2``, legacy files still decrypt); pillage passes the image format to ``qemu-nbd`` (new ``pillage.image_format`` option and ``--image-format`` flag) and refuses images that reference other files; paramiko, cryptography and lxml are updated and a ``dependency-audit`` CI job runs pip-audit; catastrophic-backtracking regexes in the SEL and FortiGate parsers are fixed.
